              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "While the very low reduction potential for lithium indicates it is capable of protecting the other metals, this also indicates how highly reactive lithium is. Lithium would have a spontaneous reaction with most substances, even those that would not oxidize the metal it is attempting to protect. This means the sacrificial anode would be depleted rapidly and need to be replaced frequently. (Optional additional reason: fire hazard in the presence of water.)"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "pobpr2xwq9rnxku",
